# AllN1 Psych — Cursor Rules
# This file is read by Cursor before every prompt. It is the source of truth.

## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING
AllN1 Psych is a **Human Life Operating System** — like a cockpit for being human. Relationships are one major subsystem, not the entire product. The system answers: *"How am I doing as a human?"* — connection, meaning, alignment — not just productivity, money, or tasks.

It teaches about emotions, listens without judgment via AI, and connects people who love each other (temperature system). It is NOT a therapy app, NOT a meditation app, NOT a mood tracker. It is the life manual nobody ever gave you. It helps people who will NEVER do therapy — which is most humans.

**Design rule:** Even when the system is big, the UI must feel simple. Keep the main pillars clear.

## TECH STACK (Do not deviate)
- Expo SDK 54 + React Native + TypeScript
- Expo Router (file-based navigation)
- Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Realtime + Storage)
- React Query (@tanstack/react-query) for data fetching
- Zustand for local state management
- Expo AV for voice recording
- Voice transcription via Whisper API or Deepgram
- AI conversations via OpenAI or Claude API
- Expo Notifications for push notifications

## APP STRUCTURE — Six tabs (life control panel)
1. **Cockpit** — Life overview. Social health, energy, important signals, upcoming obligations, drifting relationships, opportunities. Life radar.
2. **Signals** — Insights & predictions hub (awareness layer). All signals in one place: relationship drift, birthdays, social health, predictions, gauge trajectory. Easy access, well organized. Links to People and Tools for action.
3. **People** — Relationship subsystem. Dunbar tiers (5/15/50/150), temperatures, drift detection, Transmit, constellation/radar. A major subsystem, not the whole app.
4. **Tools** — Action layer. Reach out, plan hangout, send message, schedule, write note, capture idea. Converts signals → actions.
5. **Manual** — Human handbook. Friendship science, communication, conflict resolution, personal growth, social dynamics, psychology. "How to operate a human life."
6. **Me** — Personal system. Values, goals, identity, emotional state, personal metrics (energy, focus, mood, purpose). Profile, journal, settings, crisis resources.

Signals tab = single place for all insights and predictions; People tab = relationship actions and detail. Deep links to the relationship hub use the People tab.

**Alignment:** The system tracks alignment between you, your relationships, your goals, and your actions. When misalignment appears → signal. Most life apps track tasks; this system tracks human life dynamics.

## FILE STRUCTURE
```
app/
  (tabs)/
    index.tsx          # Home dashboard
    talk.tsx           # AI companion (voice-first)
    learn.tsx          # Education modules
    circle.tsx         # Temperature & connections
    me.tsx             # Profile, journal, settings
    _layout.tsx        # Tab navigator
  (modals)/
    onboarding.tsx     # First-time setup flow
    role-play.tsx      # Role play session
    mood-checkin.tsx   # Quick mood popup
    crisis.tsx         # Crisis resources
    invite-circle.tsx  # Circle invitation flow
    _layout.tsx
  _layout.tsx          # Root layout
src/
  components/
    ui/                # Reusable UI (buttons, cards, inputs)
    talk/              # Talk screen components (mic button, bubbles, waveform)
    circle/            # Temperature gauge, circle cards, nudge cards
    learn/             # Lesson cards, module cards, progress bars
    home/              # Dashboard cards, quick actions
  services/
    ai.ts              # AI conversation service (OpenAI/Claude API)
    voice.ts           # Voice recording, transcription, TTS
    temperature.ts     # Temperature calculation logic
    notifications.ts   # Push notification service
  hooks/
    useConversation.ts
    useMoodCheckin.ts
    useTemperature.ts
    useCircle.ts
    useEducation.ts
    useVoice.ts
  providers/
    AuthProvider.tsx
    QueryProvider.tsx
    ThemeProvider.tsx
  lib/
    supabase.ts        # Supabase client
    constants.ts       # App config, colors, theme
    types.ts           # TypeScript types
docs/
  supabase-schema.sql  # Database schema
  temperature-algorithm.md
```

## DESIGN SYSTEM
- **Primary Background:** Deep Dark #0F0B1E (feels safe, like nighttime)
- **Surface:** #1A1528 (cards, inputs)
- **Accent:** Calm Lavender #7C4DFF
- **Accent Light:** #B388FF
- **Success/Green Temp:** #66BB6A
- **Warning/Yellow Temp:** #FDD835
- **Orange Temp:** #FFA726
- **Red/Crisis Temp:** #EF5350
- **Text Primary:** #F5F5F7
- **Text Secondary:** #9E9E9E
- **Typography:** System fonts (San Francisco on iOS, Roboto on Android) for maximum readability and trust. Do NOT use fancy display fonts — this app is about clarity and safety.
- **Border Radius:** 16px for cards, 24px for buttons, 50% for avatars
- **Spacing:** 8px base unit
- **Tone:** Warm, safe, non-clinical. This should feel like a cozy room, not a doctor's office.

## VOICE-FIRST PRINCIPLES
- The Talk screen mic button should be LARGE and centered — it's the primary interaction
- When recording, show a waveform animation
- AI responds with text bubbles AND voice (TTS)
- Text input is always available as a toggle, never hidden
- Voice is the DEFAULT, text is the backup

## AI COMPANION BEHAVIOR
- Adapts communication style to user's age and developmental level
- Remembers all past conversations (send relevant history as context)
- Validates emotions first, advises second
- Asks permission before giving advice: "Want my thoughts, or do you just need me to listen?"
- Uses the user's love language for encouragement
- NEVER judges, minimizes, or dismisses
- References past conversations: "Last time you felt this way was..."
- For kids (8-12): simple language, metaphors, stories
- For teens (13-17): respectful, not condescending, acknowledges their world
- For adults (18+): deeper analysis, self-reflection tools
- For older adults (60+): companionship-focused, warm

## TEMPERATURE SYSTEM
- Calculated from: mood check-ins, conversation sentiment, usage patterns, user-reported events
- Shared as simple color: Green (doing well), Yellow (could use love), Orange (hard time), Red (struggling)
- Circle members get gentle nudges: "Your [relationship] could use a check-in" — NEVER specifics
- User ALWAYS controls sharing (opt-in, can pause anytime without notifying)
- Works for ANY relationship: parent-child, sibling, friend, spouse, mentor, adult child-aging parent

## SAFETY PROTOCOL
- Monitor for crisis keywords/patterns
- If detected, gently ask: "Are you having thoughts of hurting yourself?"
- Provide 988 Lifeline, Crisis Text Line (741741), 911
- NEVER diagnose, prescribe, or replace professional help
- Always include disclaimer: "I'm an AI companion, not a licensed therapist"

## CRITICAL RULES
- NEVER use business/corporate language or components
- NEVER make it feel clinical or medical
- ALWAYS prioritize privacy — conversations are sacred
- ALWAYS make voice the primary interaction
- ALWAYS adapt to user's age/developmental level
- Onboarding must feel like a genuine conversation, not a form
- Free tier must be genuinely useful (not a crippled teaser)
- This app saves lives. Build it like it matters. Because it does.

## VISUALIZATION & EXTENSIBILITY
- The Constellation/radar visualization (People) is the signature relationship view. The same UI language (layers, nodes, drift, attention) can extend to other life systems later: goals, habits, projects — so the product feels like one coherent "human dashboard" rather than separate apps.

